            <ArticleTitle>Patient-controlled analgesia--the need for caution. A case report and review of adverse incidents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>770-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Respiratory depression and oversedation occurred during the administration of patient-controlled analgesia because of a broken syringe barrel. Possible complications in the use of patient-controlled analgesia are reviewed. These may be because of prescription or provision errors, patient factors or equipment problems.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
